    {
      "field_name": "other_symptoms_established",
      "value": "stiffness; spasms; startle; anxiety; vertigo; imbalance; back pain; blurry vision; gait ataxia; neck stiffness; headache; nausea; hyperventilation; blank staring look; hip pain; spasticity",
      "quote": "She appeared anxious and her vital signs were within normal limits. Her neurological examination was essentially unremarkable except for bilateral gaze evoked nystagmus, more on the right side, and gait ataxia. Over the course of a four-day hospitalization, she underwent MRI of the brain and echocardiogram which were normal. While in hospital, she also had an episode of hyperventilation and blank staring look, which was attributed to panic episode at that time... Her symptoms of vertigo and back pain along with nausea and headache persisted after being discharged. She also had blurry vision, gait ataxia, and neck stiffness... She also had diffuse headache with giddiness along with back spasms and left leg weakness... Unable to stand and ambulate without assistance and had severe tenderness in her neck and back muscles, along with tightness and stiffness in the trapezius... Notable, she was always keeping her left leg in a flexed position and complained of pain on moving the left hip... Her symptoms improved dramatically, with progressive increase in muscle strength and mobility and decrease in hip pain and spasticity.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
