      "confidence": "medium"
    },
    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_criteria",
      "value": "clinical features such as stiffness/spasms/hyperlordosis, positive antibodies such as anti-GAD, EMG showing continuous motor-unit activity, response to benzodiazepines",
      "quote": "Treatment involves the use of GABAergic drugs such as benzodiazepines, along with corticosteroids, plasmapheresis, and intravenous immune globulin. The pathophysiology is not completely understood, but is widely believed to be associated with the involvement of anti-glutamic acid decarboxylase (anti-GAD)... Anti-glutamic acid decarboxylase (GAD 65) antibodies were markedly elevated at >2000I U/mL (normal <10 IU/mL). This along with the constellation of characteristic symptoms established the diagnosis of SPS.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
